        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aed4944f-2d29-5a53-b112-2b80bb7b14c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Second Battle of Guam, First Battle of Guam, Battle of Antietam, Maryland Campaign\n- Places: Guam, Mariana Islands, Agat, Sharpsburg, Maryland, Antietam Creek, Hoffman Farm\n- Organizations: United States, Japan\n- Topics: Pacific campaign of World War II, American Civil War\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Antietam, also called the Battle of Sharpsburg in the South, was fought on September 17, 1862, near Sharpsburg, Maryland, and Antietam Creek as part of the Maryland Campaign.\n- Hoffman Farm’s buildings were used as a hospital during the Battle of Antietam from September 17, 1862, through the following month.\n- Japan captured Guam, a U.S. territory in the Mariana Islands, from the United States in the 1941 First Battle of Guam during the Pacific campaign of World War II.\n- The Second Battle of Guam was fought from July 21 to August 10, 1944, as the American recapture of Japanese-held Guam.\n- The beaches of Agat were one of the American landing sites in the 1944 Battle of Guam, in which Guam was retaken from occupying Japanese forces.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8b6a3908-63fb-5418-8d91-ed57a6790e1d",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Guam (1944). Sentence: The Second Battle of Guam (21 July – 10 August 1944) was the American recapture of the Japanese-held island of Guam, a U.S. territory in the Mariana Islands captured by the Japanese from the U.S. in the 1941 First Battle of Guam during the Pacific campaign of World War II.\nPage: Battle of Antietam. Sentence: The Battle of Antietam , also known as the Battle of Sharpsburg, particularly in the South, was fought on September 17, 1862, near Sharpsburg, Maryland and Antietam Creek as part of the Maryland Campaign.\nPage: Agat Invasion Beach. Sentence: The beaches of Agat were one of the landing sites of American forces in the 1944 Battle of Guam, in which the island was retaken from occupying Japanese forces.\nPage: Hoffman Farm. Sentence: The farm buildings were used as a hospital during the American Civil War in Battle of Antietam from the day of the battle on September 17, 1862, and through the following month.",
